  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Percentage difference between official and average market exchange rate</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-12-08" value="450.00" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-12-08"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="10.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;This indicator was achieved as of March 2021 and continues to exceed its original target. &amp;nbsp;The official and market exchangerate were almost unified since June 2022.&amp;nbsp; Following the successful unification of the official and market exchange rate, the Government has completed the exchange rate reform by realigning the customs exchange rate to the market rate since June 2021. The realignment of the customs exchange rate is not part of the prior actions of this operation, reflecting strong government&amp;rsquo;s commitment to unifying all exchange rates.&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="2.10"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Percent of the population having received a SFSP transfer</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-12-31" value="0.00" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="40.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;While this insicator was partially achieved, there was a 12 precent increase in the number of SFSP benenifciaries receiving cashtrasfer. However, assessing &amp;nbsp;progress achieved under this pillar against the SFSP Investment Project Fianacing &amp;nbsp;Phase 1 (P173521) &amp;nbsp;indicates the &amp;nbsp;4.7 million Sudabese that received SFSP transfer represents &amp;nbsp;more than 40 percent of the target of 11.3 million people specified in the SFSP Project Results Faremwork &amp;nbsp;(page 57). There is strong indication of sustainability, given the high level of registration achieved (9.3 million people), and the government commitment to continue implementation of the SFSP beyond the operation&amp;rsquo;s closing.&amp;nbsp; In addition, an emergency project under STARS, or the Sudan Emergency Safety Nets Project (P178989) will continue providing cash transfers and food. &amp;nbsp;Progress achieved under this pillar is also assessed against the counterfactual (i.e., what would have happened in the absence of the SFSP program.) Although only 4.7 million were coved by the SFSP out of the targeted 16 million people, indications are poverty would have been worse or the 4.7 million people would have been poorer in the absence of the trasfer given Sudan&amp;rsquo;s high level of food insecurity caused by a poor 2020-2021 harvest together with substantial declines in national cereal production, as well as rising international food prices. &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="12.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Percentage share of central government expenditure on fuel subsidies in total budgetary expenditures</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-12-31" value="35.00" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="15.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;This indicator was achieved as of December 2021, as evidenced by an indicator perfomrance of nearly half the target of 15 percent. This result has been sustained beyond the operation&amp;rsquo;s closing date.&amp;nbsp; The percentage share of central government expenditure on fuel subsidies out of&amp;nbsp;total budgetary expenditures declined further from 8.2 percent in 2021 to 6.0 percent over January-June 2022,&amp;nbsp;reflecting strong government&amp;nbsp;commitment and ownership to&amp;nbsp;phasing out fuel subsidies.&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="8.20"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
 </iati-activity>
